; bfsodium KECCAK SPONGE 136 : absorb at rate 136 and squeeze as much as is asked
;
; HAND WRITTEN; FIPS 202 section 4's sponge over keccak/permute1600  at the rate
; that SHA3_256 and SHAKE256 share; The permutation is PASTED  and entered once
; per block of the padded message and once more for every rate of output after
; the first;
;
; INTERFACE entry=560 exit=1024 footprint=0:1591
; IO  in:  pad{1}  mlen{2} LE  olen{2} LE  plen{2} LE  pbuf{544}  slen{2} LE  sbuf{8}
;          then mlen bytes from the wire
;     out: olen bytes  as they come off the state
;
; THE RATE CANNOT BE A PARAMETER BUT THE PADDING BYTE CAN  which is the whole
; reason this file exists; A rate decides how many lanes the absorb touches and
; how far every one of its journeys runs  and a journey of a computed length
; needs an index  which this library does not have; A padding byte is one cell
; of data; So the two functions that share the rate 136 share this file and hand
; it their own byte: 6 for SHA3_256 and 31 for SHAKE256  and later 4 for the
; cSHAKE and KMAC pair at the same rate;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x0c7  S{200}  the sponge state; it starts at NOUGHT  which is why
;                         the five bytes read below are moved up out of it
;   @0x0c8        save    keccak/rotstate borrows this one cell and hands it
;                         back at nought  so it costs the permutation nothing
;                         and needs no room of its own
;   @0x0c8:0x330  keccak/permute1600's frame  pasted at this file's own zero
;   @0x338:0x3bf  BB{136} the block being filled; one RATE of the sponge
;   @0x3c8:0x3ed  the exclusive or frame; xor64 pasted at @0x3c8
;   @0x3f0        mlo     message bytes still to come  low byte
;   @0x3f1        mhi     and high byte
;   @0x3f2        msgleft one while either of those is not nought
;   @0x3f3        pad     one until the padding byte has been placed
;   @0x3f4        more    one while another block is wanted
;   @0x3f5        ic      the hundred and thirty six bytes of a block  and later
;                         the two hundred cells of one turn of the state
;   @0x3f6:0x3fb  t0 t1 e0 t2 t3 e1  the cells the tests are made through
;   @0x3fc        last    one if the padding byte was placed in THIS block
;   @0x3fd        olo     output bytes still owed  low byte
;   @0x3fe        ohi     and high byte
;   @0x3ff        padb    the padding byte  as it came in on the wire
;   @0x400        oleft   one while either olo or ohi is not nought
;   @0x401        kc      bytes still allowed out of the rate in hand
;   @0x402        sleft   one while the suffix still has a byte to give
;   @0x403        selse   one until the suffix arm has fired  so the
;                         padding does not fire on the same byte
;   @0x404:0x405  st0 st1 the cells the suffix tests are made through
;   @0x406:0x407  slen{2} how much suffix the sponge takes from the tape
;   @0x408:0x409  plen{2} and how much prefix; both counts are SPENT
;   @0x40a:0x40d  the prefix's own else arm  test cells and flag
;   @0x410:0x62f  pbuf{544} the prefix buffer  FOUR whole rates of it
;                         two of them are cSHAKE's own block and KMAC's
;                         key block; the other two are the room
;                         TupleHash needs for its encoded elements
;   @0x630:0x637  sbuf{8} the suffix buffer; right_encode of a length is
;                         at most five bytes  and eight is the round
;                         number above it
;
; THE RATE IS A HUNDRED AND THIRTY SIX and that is exactly SEVENTEEN LANES  so
; absorbing a block is seventeen entries of xor64 rather than a hundred and
; thirty six byte exclusive ors; Every rate in the family divides by eight the
; same way: 168 for SHAKE128 is twenty one lanes  144 for SHA3_224 is eighteen
; and 72 for SHA3_512 is nine;
;
; AND EVERY OPERAND IS MOVED  never copied  which is the one place this file is
; cheaper than keccak/theta: the state lane is replaced by the answer and the
; block is spent  so nothing needs handing back;
;
; THE BLOCK IS FILLED BY A CONVEYOR  because there is no index: a byte always
; enters at the TOP of the block and the block slides down one before the next
; one arrives; So the byte that enters first has slid a hundred and thirty five
; times when the block is full and comes to rest at the bottom  which is where
; it belongs; poly1305/absorb fills its sixteen byte block the same way;
;
; AND THE BLOCK'S BYTES COME FROM FOUR PLACES IN ORDER  which is the one
; thing to know before reading the byte source below: the TAPE PREFIX  then
; the WIRE  then the TAPE SUFFIX  then the padding; cSHAKE and KMAC put whole
; bytepad blocks in front of the message and KMAC puts right_encode of the
; output length behind it  and neither is on the wire; Each tape arm is a
; SECOND CONVEYOR feeding the first  so the block machinery below is the same
; in all four cases and only the source of the next byte differs;
;
; NOTHING IN THE BLOCK ACCOUNTING KNOWS ABOUT ANY OF THEM  and that is why a
; suffix may spill into a block of its own: whether another block is wanted is
; decided by pad  which stays set until the padding byte is placed  and the
; padding waits behind the suffix;
;
; THE PADDING IS FIPS 202's  and the conveyor makes it almost free: when the
; message runs out the next byte to enter is the padding byte  and after that
; nothing enters at all  which leaves noughts behind the conveyor exactly as the
; rule wants; The last byte of the LAST block then gains 128; That byte is either
; nought or the padding byte itself  and none of 6 and 31 and 4 carries when 128
; is added  so the case where the message is a whole number of blocks needs no
; special arm: the padding simply gets a block of its own;
;
; ON THE LAST BLOCK AND NOT ON EVERY BLOCK  which is worth saying because the
; first version of this code did it on every one and only failed once a message
; was long enough to need two; The block in which the padding byte was placed is
; the last block by definition  so placing it sets a flag and the 128 is added
; under that flag;
;
; AND THE SQUEEZE IS A LOOP  which is what SHAKE needs and SHA3 does not: the
; output may be longer than one rate  so the state is stirred again between one
; rate and the next; Within a rate the byte to go out is always the BOTTOM cell
; of the state  because keccak/rotstate turns the state over one cell at a time;
; Two hundred turns put it back exactly as the permutation left it  so a rate is
; squeezed by turning the state over all two hundred of its cells and sending a
; byte out on the first hundred and thirty six of those turns  or on as many of
; them as are still owed;
;
; AND THE STIR COMES AFTER THE RATE AND NOT BEFORE IT  under a test of whether
; anything is still owed  so a caller that asks for a rate or less pays for the
; permutation the absorb already did and not one more;
;
; A BLOCK IS ABOUT TWO AND A HALF BILLION INSTRUCTIONS  nearly all of it the
; permutation at two thousand four hundred and eighty four million  so nothing
; else in this file is worth optimising until that is; The conveyor that fills a
; block costs about five million and the absorb twenty five  and one whole turn
; of the state to squeeze a rate is thirty six million  which together are under
; three per cent of it;
;
; The five bytes of the head are read into the bottom of the STATE and moved up
; out of it  because a read prologue may hold nothing but commas and steps and
; the state must start at nought; Every distance below was worked out from the
; map;

; read the padding byte  the message length  the output length  the prefix
; length  the prefix buffer  the suffix length and the suffix buffer
